Likutay Halachos &middot; Orach Chaim

Hilchos Rosh HaShanah

And the main t&rsquo;shuvah is in the aspect of &ldquo;Dom before Hashem and wait longingly for Him, and He will fell your chalalim&rdquo; &mdash; that the blood in the left chamber is subdued, etc. And this is the aspect of the blowing of the Shofar, which is a kol without dibbur [a voice without speech] &mdash; this is the aspect of &ldquo;Dom before Hashem,&rdquo; etc., for &ldquo;we have no mouth to respond,&rdquo; etc. As is written in the holy Zohar, in Ra&rsquo;aya M&rsquo;haimnah (Mishpatim 119a): that one needs to come before Him, blessed be He, and make oneself like a b&rsquo;haimah [animal] for a korban [sacrifice], and say thus: &ldquo;I have no mouth to respond.&rdquo;

And this is the aspect of the Shofar, which is a kol without dibbur. For the Shofar is the aspect of t&rsquo;shuvah, as is brought (LM siman 60, part 1; Zohar Emor 100; Hashmasos 254; ZC Noach 34b) &mdash; the aspect of &ldquo;Awaken, you sleepers, from your slumber.&rdquo; And because at Rosh HaShanah it is the beginning of the t&rsquo;shuvah of the entire year, and at the beginning of the t&rsquo;shuvah, when a person begins to draw close to Him, blessed be He, then the accusation is very great, Rachamana litzlan [may the Merciful One save us], because his sins still divide between him and his Maker, and they accuse him and do not allow him to draw close. And then, from the greatness of the accusation, it is impossible to speak any dibbur before Him, blessed be He. For the blood in the left chamber is still in its full force, and the dibbur comes from the blood [damim], and because the blood in the left chamber is still in its force, it is impossible to speak any proper dibbur as is fitting. For the dibbur is very confused because of the blood in the left chamber.

And therefore, through the dibbur, the accusation could, chas v&rsquo;shalom, grow even stronger &mdash; especially since the accusation is then great, as above. And this is [the reason] that our Sages, of blessed memory, forbade mentioning any confession of sins on Rosh HaShanah. For on Rosh HaShanah, Eisav comes from his side, wishing to accuse, and brings all the sins, chas v&rsquo;shalom, to accuse. And from the severity of the judgment at that time, it is forbidden to mention any sin or transgression, lest [the accusation] grow stronger, chas v&rsquo;shalom, as above. For then it is the beginning of the t&rsquo;shuvah, as above.

And therefore He gives them counsel to blow the Shofar &mdash; this is the aspect of &ldquo;Dom before Hashem&rdquo;. For then, on Rosh HaShanah, one needs to be silent and quiet and not increase in speech (as Rabbainu, of blessed memory, wrote in another place). And even the sins it is forbidden to mention, as above. And this is the aspect of &ldquo;Dom before Hashem.&rdquo; And this is the aspect of the blowing of the Shofar, which is the aspect of t&rsquo;shuvah &mdash; this is the aspect of &ldquo;Dom before Hashem.&rdquo; For we have no mouth to respond, and we cannot speak any dibbur to request from before Him regarding our sins. Rather, we only call to Him, blessed be He, with a kol alone, without dibbur, in the aspect of &ldquo;From the depths I called to You, Hashem&rdquo; (T&rsquo;hillim 130:1) &mdash; from the depths of the heart. And this is the aspect of the kol of the Shofar, the aspect of &ldquo;From the narrow place I called to Y-ah.&rdquo;
